// lean_single_compound_assign_rejected
//@ compile-fail
//@ requires: lean_single
//@ error-pattern: E260
//@ description: lean_single refuses `x += e` instead of compiling it as a discarded expression
//
// Measured 2026-09-13 on bin/souc-lean-single-x86_64: this program compiled
// cleanly and printed `1.500000`. lean_single has no compound-assignment
// token, so `x += 1.0` lexed as `x` `+` `=` `1.0`, fell through compile_stmt
// (and compile_stmt_a64) to the expression-statement arm, and `x` was never
// written. Same for `-=`, `*=`, `/=`. The engine now refuses the form (E260).
//
// `requires: lean_single` because Madaros parses compound assignment (AssignOp)
// and accepts this program, so the diagnostic is engine-specific.

fn main() with IO {
    var x = 1.5
    x += 1.0
    println(x)
}
